    "zh": "短讲结束后，你将有三分钟检查作答。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "check"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen014.png",
    "sha256": "9b5f841704831abfa242c1b3d7a1b1a106c541fc34d4cf0e82b0aea2db003ea7",
    "k": 13,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": "transition",
    "en": "Metaphors in speaking.",
    "zh": "讲话中的隐喻。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "metaphor"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen015.png",
    "sha256": "739348103224cf2449ec4d014c02edb81747d4726517508e81bda1a1f2068ed3",
    "k": 14,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "Good morning, everyone.",
    "zh": "大家早上好。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "Good morning"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen016.png",
    "sha256": "3ca041c2b022507431d6aaf0c95326e21f30bbac2d4c658a33afcbff1df79add",
    "k": 15,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "Today we’ll continue our discussion on the art of speaking, focusing on the use of metaphors in speaking.",
    "zh": "今天我们继续讨论说话的艺术，重点谈谈说话时隐喻的运用。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "art of speaking",
      "metaphor"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen017.png",
    "sha256": "b7f86303a95a74d0fa3d994c08dcb9df8f4e87bd2f4ac15aca67763d2f9c92b5",
    "k": 16,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "Now, why do we need to talk about metaphors in speaking?",
    "zh": "那么，我们为什么需要讨论说话时的隐喻呢？",
    "vocabulary": [
      "metaphor"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen018.png",
    "sha256": "a2dc8b3ccd7c8fa973339076a2f843414af114c5b289c244c315b61be7bd3131",
    "k": 17,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "Well, according to research findings, we utter about six metaphors a minute.",
    "zh": "研究发现，我们平均每分钟会说出大约六个隐喻。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "research findings",
      "utter"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen019.png",
    "sha256": "7e81c1faced097898c512e5442a116732ef94f13d03a6b9c35946ad2358ecd18",
    "k": 18,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "And metaphorical thinking is essential to how we understand ourselves and others, how we communicate, learn, discover and invent.",
    "zh": "隐喻思维对于我们理解自己和他人，以及交流、学习、发现和发明，都至关重要。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "metaphorical",
      "be essential to"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen020.png",
    "sha256": "67e0f8109bab62794a1d43145969a228ccb24720df73e4bf724e85d8a247e186",
    "k": 19,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "Actually, metaphor is a way of thought before it is a way with words.",
    "zh": "实际上，隐喻首先是一种思维方式，然后才是一种语言表达方式。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "a way of thought",
      "a way with words"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen021.png",
    "sha256": "e64288617b327a7646f42845be1f1ae2b9a2ed77a2e76f832650a022dfa94046",
    "k": 20,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "Now, to assist me in explaining this, I've enlisted the help of a man whose contributions to the field are so tremendous that he himself has become a metaphor.",
    "zh": "为了帮助解释这一点，我请来了一位男士助阵；他对这个领域的贡献如此巨大，以至于他本人都已成为一个隐喻。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "enlist",
      "contribution",
      "tremendous"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen022.png",
    "sha256": "e5fbd5e3cfbe9ed68795a03a6c1bad7c82bc67591fc99f5ac0a98a5ae335f353",
    "k": 21,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "I am, of course, referring to none other than Elvis Presley.",
    "zh": "当然，我说的正是“猫王”埃尔维斯·普雷斯利。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "refer to",
      "none other than"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen023.png",
    "sha256": "e1df9ef02d4082955510c97f54ce868a2d468b56a9d0462bf573c5cc6aafcb2a",
    "k": 22,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "His All Shook Up is such a touching love song.",
    "zh": "他的《All Shook Up》是一首十分动人的情歌。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "touching",
      "love song"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen024.png",
    "sha256": "4dbf7bec0bbdb981f352528c3cda9727bfa4cf2dde11114a83a90ca78be8d758",
    "k": 23,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "It’s also an example of how we inevitably resort to metaphor when we deal with anything abstract, like ideas, emotions, feelings, concepts, thoughts.",
    "zh": "这首歌也说明，当我们处理观念、情绪、感受、概念和思想等抽象事物时，总会不可避免地借助隐喻。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "inevitably",
      "resort to",
      "abstract"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen025.png",
    "sha256": "fa82a484aa41ae9be25ae85ff1224a5b6fdf5bdc18bede49bf89430a55b925fd",
    "k": 24,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "In this, Elvis is following Aristotle’s classic definition of metaphor, that is, metaphor is the process of giving the thing a name that belongs to something else.",
    "zh": "在这里，猫王遵循了亚里士多德对隐喻的经典定义：隐喻，就是把原本属于其他事物的名称赋予某个事物的过程。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "classic",
      "definition",
      "belong to"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen026.png",
    "sha256": "d07aa3d129ae97726cd71f37e4b03e1963f1c242c351acd99fce39594cf60cec",
    "k": 25,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "And this is the mathematics of metaphor.",
    "zh": "这就是隐喻的数学表达。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "mathematics"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen027.png",
    "sha256": "486c79332b04f7e22246a26d35a23a3440c5e992389cb05e20a3cca805759ccc",
    "k": 26,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "X equals Y.",
    "zh": "X等于Y。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "equal"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen028.png",
    "sha256": "c3d0651acfd9c8834e456b9f8edfe5e366db8c2450059e1df3ac6884be404dfa",
    "k": 27,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "It’s very simple, isn’t it?",
    "zh": "很简单，对不对？",
    "vocabulary": [
      "simple"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen029.png",
    "sha256": "b20f35bf7557dd332a49f1b4a9a7c377b27eee914b0bd80211b61edbbd007172",
    "k": 28,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "This formula works wherever metaphor is present.",
    "zh": "只要存在隐喻，这个公式就适用。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "formula",
      "present"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen030.png",
    "sha256": "9a643a46fcc82c33eadee50d85e9fa71d2cf8ca2d083d75760d9255ee669ecc0",
    "k": 29,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "Elvis used metaphor, and so does Shakespeare in this famous line from Romeo and Juliet, that is, “Juliet is the sun.”",
    "zh": "猫王运用了隐喻，莎士比亚在《罗密欧与朱丽叶》的这句名言中也运用了隐喻：“朱丽叶就是太阳。”",
    "vocabulary": [
      "metaphor",
      "famous line"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen031.png",
    "sha256": "5958f9984cee9a11ff3c8961eb9aaad79e1b73dc8cbda22444b3fc7d86aeeb60",
    "k": 30,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "Now here, Shakespeare gives the thing, Juliet, a name that belongs to something else, the sun.",
    "zh": "这里，莎士比亚给朱丽叶这个人物赋予了一个属于另一事物的名称——太阳。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "belong to"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen032.png",
    "sha256": "56f29cbac80728fb9c85f39664b9b059c5dd2b2e0cfb39d1f17408c4cb260309",
    "k": 31,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "In fact, whenever we give a thing a name that belongs to something else, we give it a whole network of analogies too.",
    "zh": "实际上，每当我们用另一个事物的名称来称呼某个事物时，也为它赋予了一整套类比关系。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "network of analogies"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen033.png",
    "sha256": "fdb8fe34d2cd98a5e75615e8043fd1f4d606a1d60d613f83fa906c7930996c5a",
    "k": 32,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "We mix and match what we know about the metaphor’s source, in this case, the sun, with what we know about its target, Juliet.",
    "zh": "我们把自己对隐喻源域的认识——这里是对太阳的认识，与对目标域朱丽叶的认识，进行组合搭配。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "mix and match",
      "source",
      "target"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen034.png",
    "sha256": "44818958269d41a431f55a8a4fb0087047104332662168dc260d061d14d6fd37",
    "k": 33,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "And metaphor gives us a much more vivid understanding of Juliet than if Shakespeare had literally described just what she looks like.",
    "zh": "相比莎士比亚直接描述朱丽叶的外貌，隐喻让我们对她产生了更加生动的认识。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "vivid",
      "literally"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen035.png",
    "sha256": "39665236ad7dd10daa35a7738ba47c57d46bfc152d3016bbb6acb02fd98fb9dc",
    "k": 34,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "So how do we make and interpret metaphors?",
    "zh": "那么，我们是怎样创造和理解隐喻的呢？",
    "vocabulary": [
      "interpret"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen036.png",
    "sha256": "654f856d7e4a6fc3de5f37b743bdcbb18d5bb82fd4cb61aca4cc17fcc8dbb291",
    "k": 35,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "This might look familiar.",
    "zh": "这看起来可能很熟悉。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "familiar"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen037.png",
    "sha256": "6aaef6ff38d19110dd400d28e175b1a4eed7916cf20f32b83c60b87d3c4039bb",
    "k": 36,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "The first step is pattern recognition.",
    "zh": "第一步是模式识别。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "pattern recognition"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen038.png",
    "sha256": "b4717806ec1898928a0ace055679de83e13106383b6f20459e41cabcd09f0e7c",
    "k": 37,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "Metaphor is not just the detection of patterns; instead, it is the creation of patterns.",
    "zh": "隐喻不只是识别模式，更是在创造模式。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "detection",
      "creation"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen039.png",
    "sha256": "685788153fd71946ebd637b2f09ca86649091dd0f22596bb56e13f8879bdaad7",
    "k": 38,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "And the second step is conceptual synesthesia.",
    "zh": "第二步是概念联觉。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "conceptual synesthesia"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen040.png",
    "sha256": "b05834cfe892607c5af875da7265f81c01435100066dde9d59db47ca88dea072",
    "k": 39,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "And what is synesthesia?",
    "zh": "什么是联觉呢？",
    "vocabulary": [
      "synesthesia"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen041.png",
    "sha256": "41e923f870ec3eedb0b3a4d9dd415c1dfe54253352f78955dc7e9b187ec64707",
    "k": 40,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "It is the experience of a stimulus received by one sense organ in another sense organ as well, for example, like colored hearing.",
    "zh": "联觉是指一种感觉器官接收到的刺激，也在另一种感觉器官中产生感受的体验，例如色听联觉。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "stimulus",
      "sense organ",
      "colored hearing"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen042.png",
    "sha256": "4443d5602c7728162a14c513ca4c88ef4f2d288df08564d704a1652a6e61678b",
    "k": 41,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "People with colored hearing actually see colors when they hear the sounds of words or letters.",
    "zh": "有色听联觉的人，在听到单词或字母的声音时，真的会看到颜色。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "colored hearing"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen043.png",
    "sha256": "90f8437ce5cd018d6783b6f45d3d4a957fef0d7cbeb5532a68f1d5b22b90f200",
    "k": 42,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "We all have synesthetic abilities, and many of the metaphors we use every day are synesthetic.",
    "zh": "我们都具有联觉能力，而日常使用的许多隐喻都具有联觉性质。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "synesthetic"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen044.png",
    "sha256": "975ba4d6f54131d2c06e63a6e6ca42a4471d189b07af45f63fea7b6db323e77b",
    "k": 43,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "For instance, silence is sweet.",
    "zh": "比如，宁静是甜美的。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "sweet"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen045.png",
    "sha256": "544ef8a64de96bb68a1f536e12bf1d9f525e0bbc48b109653fc31e72c44ebe0b",
    "k": 44,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "Neckties are loud.",
    "zh": "领带是“响亮”的，也就是花哨醒目的。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "necktie",
      "loud"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen046.png",
    "sha256": "a7b0a946deb1b4d5315bd82d7c5ce980157b62fa7102be95105614e3a5f57be0",
    "k": 45,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "So metaphor creates a kind of conceptual synesthesia, in which we understand one concept in the context of another.",
    "zh": "所以，隐喻创造了一种概念联觉，让我们借助另一个概念的背景来理解一个概念。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "concept",
      "in the context of"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen047.png",
    "sha256": "c6ef94a1ddf36a1bb19f8d5efa856d1c84ab594c8277a9a1172aa54f6faead71",
    "k": 46,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "Let’s move on to the third step, that is cognitive dissonance.",
    "zh": "接着看第三步，也就是认知失调。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "cognitive dissonance"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen048.png",
    "sha256": "51bb37ed8c61838c7899af6c55a2e8c0755046760d036dfbab0e2039480e87a4",
    "k": 47,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "There is a test called the Stroop test.",
    "zh": "有一种测试叫斯特鲁普测试。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "Stroop test"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen049.png",
    "sha256": "219453ce9c52d954563d4da2ab21f6173cbd24fde7dfc4422a800fffb181ddca",
    "k": 48,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "What you need to do is identify as quickly as possible the color of the ink in which words of color are printed.",
    "zh": "你需要尽快辨认出印刷颜色词时所用墨水的颜色。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "identify",
      "ink"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen050.png",
    "sha256": "0344b929fa37c108cc3f0020a1bd9f0fc11d67f7a938b146ce774c88fe739a31",
    "k": 49,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "If you’re like most people, you’ll experience a moment of cognitive dissonance where the name of the color is printed in a differently colored ink.",
    "zh": "如果你和大多数人一样，面对用另一种颜色墨水印出的颜色名称时，会经历片刻的认知失调。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "cognitive dissonance"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen051.png",
    "sha256": "3e87da9bf387439b9b38696c277b2a97b8aeb90386afcbf5333c77b6f8db268c",
    "k": 50,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "For example, the word “red” is printed in blue ink.",
    "zh": "比如，“红”这个字用蓝色墨水印出来。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "print",
      "ink"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen052.png",
    "sha256": "2d0fe0f4eb529b31edf469e6ac3f967d312c607a94d7ab2bec515fe86ebaf73d",
    "k": 51,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "Then you may wonder what the test intends to tell us.",
    "zh": "你可能会想，这个测试究竟要告诉我们什么。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "intend to"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen053.png",
    "sha256": "6cf73a551c18bcb24738a880a5485fc40ff4f72bb1df6469ccd2773d4c4fa3d2",
    "k": 52,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "Well, the test shows that we cannot overlook the literal meaning of words, even when the literal meaning gives the wrong answer.",
    "zh": "这个测试表明，我们无法忽略词语的字面意义，即使它会导向错误答案。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "overlook",
      "literal meaning"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen054.png",
    "sha256": "0b404427842dec18dc2d91fd630b53ca01e963c9814ad08280077eb85958aea6",
    "k": 53,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "Stroop tests have been done with metaphor as well.",
    "zh": "研究人员也用隐喻做过斯特鲁普测试。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "metaphor"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen055.png",
    "sha256": "ca241d0eeb2a0f0ad407ec962b291e2e1ff4175de090a43a873444eef97999a2",
    "k": 54,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "The participants had to identify as quickly as possible the literally false sentences.",
    "zh": "参与者必须尽可能快地找出字面意义上不成立的句子。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "participant",
      "literally"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen056.png",
    "sha256": "ba5edc5eee57696e7d6c3a330f4456f072761415733795e18f3d9ded11153a13",
    "k": 55,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "They took longer to reject metaphors as false than they did to reject literally false sentences.",
    "zh": "相比其他字面意义上不成立的句子，他们需要更长时间，才能把隐喻句判定为错误。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "reject",
      "metaphor"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen057.png",
    "sha256": "47f0402cf28d588045ce3825a8f46b89e667cb81563572dc587c9cfcb4e81886",
    "k": 56,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "Why? Because we cannot ignore the metaphorical meaning of words either.",
    "zh": "为什么？因为我们同样无法忽视词语的隐喻意义。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "metaphorical meaning"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen058.png",
    "sha256": "8c037a76e63dc20b9a2d504e84e2c3ceb8a7bcb56daa033afa69b53ee06a37f9",
    "k": 57,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "For example, one of the sentences was, “Some jobs are jails.”",
    "zh": "比如，其中一句是：“有些工作就是监狱。”",
    "vocabulary": [
      "jail"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen059.png",
    "sha256": "5d1631f27a218a2e8460dc5f76e77430b4fd32adc6895e290c1300a4eec9fb5f",
    "k": 58,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "Now, unless you’re a prison guard yourself, the sentence “Some jobs are jails.” is literally false.",
    "zh": "除非你自己就是狱警，否则“有些工作就是监狱”这句话，从字面上说是不成立的。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "prison guard",
      "literally"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen060.png",
    "sha256": "23278f480e5d3aa6947dfa0b96ac2c04d737a11d07171c0a46c689eb74b4c937",
    "k": 59,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "Sadly, it’s metaphorically true.",
    "zh": "遗憾的是，从隐喻意义上说，它却是真的。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "metaphorically"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen061.png",
    "sha256": "bead37e8e6d4bce9863a22974c8e449b079e65e931e8cba039af5bf06407e771",
    "k": 60,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "And the metaphorical truth interferes with our ability to identify it as literally false.",
    "zh": "这种隐喻层面的真实，会干扰我们把它判为字面意义上不成立的句子。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "interfere with",
      "ability"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen062.png",
    "sha256": "d24d005012a413a5c91257ab86d972dea0a7c9eeb46b794501cc33a5228e3e54",
    "k": 61,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "Metaphor matters because it’s around us every day, all the time.",
    "zh": "隐喻之所以重要，是因为它每天、时时刻刻都在我们身边。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "matter"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen063.png",
    "sha256": "f68c41c0b1ff209bbf4183325d6c89b1b3a1325c001e83d51220a0765f3ea095",
    "k": 62,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "How and in what ways does metaphor matter?",
    "zh": "隐喻究竟是怎样、又在哪些方面发挥作用的？",
    "vocabulary": [
      "matter"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen064.png",
    "sha256": "0d479d8c28417aefef5e430a0e903165b0294aad8ed736b0e76bfef66d5c3bbc",
    "k": 63,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "Well, I’d say metaphor matters, first of all, because it creates expectations.",
    "zh": "首先，我认为隐喻很重要，因为它能塑造预期。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "expectation"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen065.png",
    "sha256": "f7e23f91e40b916e2a5d1ebeba9333bd51f185816dc58824698a30d0817df6af",
    "k": 64,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "So pay careful attention the next time you read some financial news.",
    "zh": "所以，下次阅读财经新闻时，请格外留心。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "pay careful attention",
      "financial news"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen066.png",
    "sha256": "69dac283c4323a21bb384281d8282125ebdbc4486e62307e8f67ade2c52acdfd",
    "k": 65,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "Agent metaphors describe price movements as the deliberate action of a living thing, as in, “The NASDAQ climbed higher.”",
    "zh": "施事隐喻把价格变动描述成生命体有意为之的动作，比如：“纳斯达克指数继续向上攀爬。”",
    "vocabulary": [
      "Agent metaphors",
      "deliberate",
      "NASDAQ"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen067.png",
    "sha256": "33bc6af10d144d0e45618d1551aca9424b3e5791a54a3d900cbc272ac41150c2",
    "k": 66,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "Object metaphors describe price movements as non-living things, as in, “The Dow fell like a brick.”",
    "zh": "物体隐喻则把价格变动描述为无生命物体的运动，比如：“道琼斯指数像砖块一样坠落。”",
    "vocabulary": [
      "Object metaphors",
      "non-living",
      "Dow"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen068.png",
    "sha256": "7b52751e7597e91fde0169eaca575f8786a5f771e57c10a7cbb011ec0d5a9b54",
    "k": 67,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "Researchers once asked a group of people to read market commentaries and then predict the next day’s price trend.",
    "zh": "研究人员曾让一组人阅读市场评论，再预测第二天的价格走势。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "commentary",
      "predict",
      "trend"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen069.png",
    "sha256": "36ed5b57a87eda4bb16eb740c2ad6f662235c2f95f82d2469599005d798c8ded",
    "k": 68,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "Those exposed to agent metaphors had higher expectations that price trends would continue.",
    "zh": "接触施事隐喻的人，更倾向于预期价格走势会持续下去。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "be exposed to",
      "expectation"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen070.png",
    "sha256": "76b7efbcba7dba9755dba5cb4f2c64f323f8b0ba91f4e3432a56e94759ba05a3",
    "k": 69,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "And they had those expectations because agent metaphors imply the deliberate action of a living thing pursuing a goal.",
    "zh": "他们之所以这样预期，是因为施事隐喻暗示：某个生命体正在有意识地采取行动，追求一个目标。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "imply",
      "pursue"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen071.png",
    "sha256": "16d676add52a976e2f6996e22455c435e322ace85bd382d674c6aa8ea17ffa34",
    "k": 70,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "If, for example, house prices are routinely described as climbing and climbing, higher and higher, people might naturally assume that rise is incessant.",
    "zh": "例如，如果房价经常被描述为不断攀升、越爬越高，人们自然可能以为上涨会永不停息。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "routinely",
      "assume",
      "incessant"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen072.png",
    "sha256": "66c1f069fbb7228fc8004388c6dac30cf3eea243966d34612dd1659e673c7516",
    "k": 71,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "Also, metaphor matters because it influences decisions by activating analogies.",
    "zh": "隐喻也很重要，因为它能激活类比，从而影响决策。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "activate",
      "analogy"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen073.png",
    "sha256": "fb4a9b43ba5797b25ed61750d281c0371fcb51c819dac7f37e81ea6bccf2d169",
    "k": 72,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "Let me give you an example, which was actually an experiment.",
    "zh": "我来举个例子，这实际上是一项实验。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "experiment"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen074.png",
    "sha256": "9bbb6526bdc8443099372b4a685790c3ae0b7de9225bff7340c5db46c558cbea",
    "k": 73,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "A group of students was told that a small country had been invaded and had asked for help.",
    "zh": "一组学生被告知：有个小国遭到入侵，并请求援助。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "invade"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen075.png",
    "sha256": "ac58eac2c675f3d86efa51234e7b5698a82022328bae4bd605109c2a3383d571",
    "k": 74,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "And they had to make a decision.",
    "zh": "他们必须作出决定。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "make a decision"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen076.png",
    "sha256": "4ff2683a2060787deab3466724d7410b973dc41e2c624ddc959db94dbb76e774",
    "k": 75,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "What should they do? Intervene, appeal to the United Nations, or just do nothing?",
    "zh": "他们该怎么办呢？进行干预、向联合国求助，还是袖手旁观？",
    "vocabulary": [
      "intervene",
      "appeal to",
      "United Nations"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen077.png",
    "sha256": "f1d1af8248700fc799615784c42bd72db275c3a27b762c0a8b82dc477ac4322c",
    "k": 76,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "They were each then given one of the three descriptions of this hypothetical crisis.",
    "zh": "随后，每名学生都收到了关于这一假设危机的三种描述之一。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "hypothetical",
      "crisis"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen078.png",
    "sha256": "634292e04c1b6572118ab7efd77892c3695e35dbb336c7164737c25e3890af0c",
    "k": 77,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "Each of the three descriptions was designed to trigger a different historical analogy: World War II, Vietnam, and the third was historically neutral.",
    "zh": "这三种描述分别旨在唤起不同的历史类比：第二次世界大战、越南战争，以及第三种不带历史指向的描述。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "trigger",
      "historical analogy",
      "neutral"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen079.png",
    "sha256": "cef18e0e735617f78ac0eeaf4fcfb6a406d78bd65fac8ae4c225bc616bc09a62",
    "k": 78,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "Those exposed to the World War II scenario made more interventionist recommendations than the others.",
    "zh": "接触到二战情境描述的人，提出了比其他人更多的干预主义建议。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "scenario",
      "interventionist",
      "recommendation"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen080.png",
    "sha256": "448ec16c9d228cbb289a8102f09881f3e027b903b3ee8c15af3cd7ba74a01aff",
    "k": 79,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "This shows that just as we cannot ignore the literal meaning of words, we cannot ignore the analogies that are triggered by metaphor.",
    "zh": "这说明，正如我们无法忽略词语的字面意义一样，也无法忽略隐喻所引发的类比。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "analogy",
      "trigger"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen081.png",
    "sha256": "819845a6865382de11d9d4d25a198760e35608fa1f89fe8fdd77ab3fc50ef5c6",
    "k": 80,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "Metaphor matters because it opens the door to discovery.",
    "zh": "隐喻很重要，因为它为新发现打开了大门。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "open the door to",
      "discovery"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen082.png",
    "sha256": "bcc0f6cedc1b1c88e80c36b04cfd4b09dc09170139223b2d194cbb995d53d174",
    "k": 81,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "Whenever we solve a problem or make a discovery, we compare what we know with what we don’t know.",
    "zh": "每当解决问题或有所发现时，我们都在比较已知与未知。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "compare"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen083.png",
    "sha256": "302bf5e8efba43cdfe4ac0369df170ddf6748ededc5d63b1b6be72f093612cd0",
    "k": 82,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "And the only way to find out about the latter is to investigate the ways it might be like the former.",
    "zh": "要了解后者，唯一的办法就是探究它可能在哪些方面与前者相似。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "the latter",
      "investigate",
      "the former"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen084.png",
    "sha256": "f8846602a33ed34c9dc09dec89fb03d65f15ea29a6aeadf1c309fc354ad10b1b",
    "k": 83,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "Now, we know that metaphor is ubiquitous, yet it’s hidden.",
    "zh": "现在我们知道，隐喻无处不在，却又隐藏着。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "ubiquitous",
      "hidden"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen085.png",
    "sha256": "d97572a49a8e9f9640e8dd30f2523540f6f457d0b4589231dad641e96c864fad",
    "k": 84,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "But you just have to look at the words around you, and you'll find it.",
    "zh": "但只要看看周围的词语，你就会发现它。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "look at"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen086.png",
    "sha256": "9fbd543a28b904411015afc7928662a8f6c02922ca8beffce7f560baa27fa402",
    "k": 85,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "Ralph Waldo Emerson described language as “fossil poetry.”",
    "zh": "拉尔夫·沃尔多·爱默生把语言描述为“化石般的诗”。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "fossil poetry"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen087.png",
    "sha256": "a8a5d11e174f42a4a544b45a83bdfe3add65a7a43f43395b777cff1e6029829d",
    "k": 86,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "But before, it was fossil metaphor, and these fossils still breathe.",
    "zh": "但在此之前，它是化石般的隐喻，而这些化石至今仍在呼吸。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "fossil metaphor",
      "breathe"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen088.png",
    "sha256": "bc7256ed713ca3d2ca6adca70cac1239f675cd40397265daa559b25c79a2f70a",
    "k": 87,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "OK, let me sum up today’s lecture.",
    "zh": "好，让我总结一下今天的讲座。",
    "vocabulary": [
